  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 202 PM MDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nSunday Night - Friday: For the rest of the forecast period, active \nweather persist across south central and southeastern Colorado. The \nridge of high pressure to south will remain there, but will slowly \nmeander further to the southwest throughout the week. While monsoon \nmoisture will continue to stream around this feature and into the \narea, it will become less and less as the high pressure cuts-off the \nbetter quality moisture heading through week. With that all said, \ndaily afternoon and evening showers and storms are still expected \neach day, with the greatest coverage through Wednesday, with a \nprogressive downtrend in coverage Thursday and Friday. Otherwise, \nwinds will continue to remain relatively light, with afternoon and \nevening clouds expected. Temperatures will also remain elevated, \nwith much of the region staying at above seasonal values through the \nweek, especially for the end of the week.",
